  "geometryBasis": "The named Coptic Museum perimeter and three museum-tagged sections plus two southern wings inside the named precinct fix the shell plan. The adjacent Hanging Church and Roman towers are independent landmarks.",
  "sectionBasis": "The museum operator describes two floors in two wings. Archival research identifies the 1929 neo-Fatimid entrance, six marble porch columns, courtyard fountain, hardwood mashrabiyas and staircase below the east cupola.",
  "limitations": [
    "The model covers the museum wings, their connecting passage, the entrance and the garden-facing courts. Nearby churches and the Roman towers have separate identities.",
    "The current building footprint follows the mapping. Wing heights, window spacing, stair shape, court locations and court floor grades are estimates based on the written architectural history.",
    "Medium-fi geometric motifs represent the recessed shell and medallions, with simplified timber latticework. The original inscriptions and sculpture are beyond this exterior model."
